263
00:20:03,386 --> 00:20:06,014
<i>What's wrong?
Wasn't this what you wanted?</i>

264
00:20:07,682 --> 00:20:09,309
<i>You don't have to feel so guilty.</i>

265
00:20:10,644 --> 00:20:11,645
Because

266
00:20:12,771 --> 00:20:13,938
I want Ha-gi back

267
00:20:15,273 --> 00:20:16,858
for myself again.

268
00:20:32,408 --> 00:20:33,868
IF YOU DON'T KNOW HAN,
YOU DON'T KNOW FASHION

269
00:20:40,082 --> 00:20:42,585
CLOTHES THAT STAY WITH YOU

270
00:20:45,796 --> 00:20:47,089
"Clothes that stay with you."

271
00:21:13,366 --> 00:21:15,076
You want to work
with a designated employee?

272
00:21:15,159 --> 00:21:18,287
Yes, it's weird to reach out
to the CEO every single time.

273
00:21:19,288 --> 00:21:22,792
Did you say it was Ms. Nam Da-reum
who wrote the proposal?

274
00:21:25,419 --> 00:21:26,420
I want her.

275
00:21:33,135 --> 00:21:35,888
- Why Ms. Da-reum of all people?
- I told you already.

276
00:21:36,222 --> 00:21:38,224
I liked Appello's proposal.

277
00:21:38,808 --> 00:21:41,894
I loved the level of understanding
she has of my brand.

278
00:21:43,896 --> 00:21:47,024
I'll see if Ms. Da-reum
will be interested.

279
00:21:47,108 --> 00:21:48,150
I can ask now.

280
00:21:58,160 --> 00:21:59,245
Ms. Nam Da-reum?

281
00:22:03,040 --> 00:22:05,209
- Yes.
- I loved your proposal.

282
00:22:06,168 --> 00:22:08,713
I need someone who'll handle
my business with Appello.

283
00:22:08,963 --> 00:22:11,757
Would you like to lead the project?

284
00:22:17,346 --> 00:22:20,141
I'd be happy to,
if Mr. Kang is okay with it.

285
00:22:21,851 --> 00:22:23,269
It's a great opportunity, I guess.

286
00:22:24,562 --> 00:22:26,063
But it's your opinion that matters.

287
00:22:28,607 --> 00:22:29,775
What do you think?

288
00:22:33,279 --> 00:22:34,405
In that case

289
00:22:36,365 --> 00:22:37,700
I want to do it.

290
00:22:39,827 --> 00:22:42,580
Excellent. I look forward to it.

291
00:23:02,099 --> 00:23:03,726
<i>You don't have to feel so guilty.</i>

292
00:23:05,269 --> 00:23:06,395
<i>Because</i>

293
00:23:07,480 --> 00:23:11,484
<i>I want Ha-gi back for myself again.</i>

294
00:23:20,451 --> 00:23:21,452
WON-BIN

295
00:23:23,078 --> 00:23:24,079
Hey, Won-bin.

296
00:23:24,163 --> 00:23:26,040
<i>I've got bad news, Chan.</i>

297
00:23:31,170 --> 00:23:32,213
You're here.

298
00:23:32,922 --> 00:23:33,923
Let's go.

299
00:23:36,675 --> 00:23:38,135
First, put these on.

300
00:23:38,469 --> 00:23:40,054
No, I didn't do anything wrong.

301
00:23:41,013 --> 00:23:44,266
You didn't leave behind
weird photos or videos, right?

302
00:23:44,725 --> 00:23:46,352
What do you take me for?

303
00:23:47,812 --> 00:23:51,190
Anyway, Jinu and Teo
were the ones who got hacked.

304
00:23:51,273 --> 00:23:54,276
Why are you getting summoned? Gosh.

305
00:23:54,360 --> 00:23:55,778
I'm nervous to death.

306
00:23:56,695 --> 00:23:57,780
There it is.

307
00:23:57,863 --> 00:24:02,117
INVESTIGATION DIVISION

308
00:24:02,409 --> 00:24:05,371
Thankfully, the hacker was arrested
before any information got leaked.

309
00:24:06,205 --> 00:24:08,541
The data he used to blackmail them

310
00:24:08,624 --> 00:24:13,254
included unreleased songs and videos
related to you, Mr. Lee.

311
00:24:13,337 --> 00:24:14,505
I wanted to check with you.

312
00:24:18,300 --> 00:24:19,468
Wait.

313
00:24:19,552 --> 00:24:22,179
These are materials you used
for your album preparations.

314
00:24:22,638 --> 00:24:24,014
It was supposedly
for the five of you.

315
00:24:25,891 --> 00:24:27,601
It must've been important.

316
00:24:27,685 --> 00:24:31,522
They even gave the hacker money
and tried to stop it.

317
00:24:35,359 --> 00:24:36,986
They tried that hard?

318
00:24:39,071 --> 00:24:40,489
And they didn't even tell me.

319
00:24:52,459 --> 00:24:53,544
Boys.

320
00:24:57,673 --> 00:24:58,716
Chan.

321
00:25:12,646 --> 00:25:15,065
You should've called me first
when this happened.

322
00:25:15,524 --> 00:25:18,986
What money did you have
to hand over to that guy?

323
00:25:19,528 --> 00:25:21,322
I mean, it included Chan's data...

324
00:25:23,407 --> 00:25:24,992
and songs you worked on for years.

325
00:25:25,075 --> 00:25:26,452
We disbanded a decade ago.

326
00:25:26,535 --> 00:25:27,953
Why are you still like this?

327
00:25:28,871 --> 00:25:30,372
Go live your life now. Please.

328
00:25:30,456 --> 00:25:32,416
You may be done, but not us.

329
00:25:33,918 --> 00:25:34,960
For us

330
00:25:35,794 --> 00:25:37,087
D.N.X is everything.

331
00:25:40,716 --> 00:25:41,717
Sorry.

332
00:25:42,468 --> 00:25:44,762
We'll try not to stand in your way
from now on.

333
00:25:46,931 --> 00:25:48,182
Hey, Jinu.

334
00:25:48,807 --> 00:25:49,808
Jinu.

335
00:26:07,743 --> 00:26:09,745
You must be working hard
for the presentation

336
00:26:10,079 --> 00:26:12,873
so I prepared this meeting
to show you my support.

337
00:26:13,165 --> 00:26:15,042
There's nothing much for us to do.

338
00:26:15,250 --> 00:26:17,962
We've caught up with Appello
as soon as our platform launched.

339
00:26:18,504 --> 00:26:20,172
We'll take first place in no time.

340
00:26:21,632 --> 00:26:25,177
And we're almost done
with customer profiling.

341
00:26:26,470 --> 00:26:30,808
HAN's customers must be those
who are drawn to scarcity.

342
00:26:39,358 --> 00:26:43,028
HAN's customers must be those
who are drawn to scarcity.

343
00:26:44,363 --> 00:26:47,366
The desire to have something
that you cannot have.

344
00:26:47,825 --> 00:26:50,828
You're right. People line up
before the opening because of that.

345
00:26:51,495 --> 00:26:52,621
Scarcity.

346
00:26:54,623 --> 00:26:55,749
Scarcity.

347
00:27:05,843 --> 00:27:07,011
Scarcity.

348
00:27:07,720 --> 00:27:09,388
We should approach the Korean market

349
00:27:09,847 --> 00:27:11,515
with the same
limited-edition strategy.

350
00:27:12,766 --> 00:27:14,268
That's an interesting take.

351
00:27:15,310 --> 00:27:16,562
What does

352
00:27:17,688 --> 00:27:19,189
Appello think?

353
00:27:23,694 --> 00:27:24,778
I can't say for sure.

354
00:27:26,238 --> 00:27:27,281
We're still

355
00:27:28,449 --> 00:27:29,491
working on it.

356
00:27:35,539 --> 00:27:37,750
Goodness. We should eat.

357
00:27:39,960 --> 00:27:41,879
It looks great.

358
00:28:00,773 --> 00:28:04,026
Something's going on between
Kang Ha-gi and Han Jeong-yeon.

359
00:28:04,359 --> 00:28:05,402
Find out what it is.

360
00:28:13,285 --> 00:28:15,537
HERITY FACTORY:
MODERN POP-UP SHOWROOM

361
00:28:20,417 --> 00:28:21,668
You're still here.

362
00:28:22,961 --> 00:28:24,755
Hey, Director Lee.

363
00:28:30,594 --> 00:28:32,679
I was passing by,
and I saw the lights on.

364
00:28:33,138 --> 00:28:35,265
If anyone is working until now,
it had to be you.

365
00:28:36,642 --> 00:28:38,519
I had to work on something.

366
00:28:39,728 --> 00:28:41,105
Don't you go on dates?

367
00:28:46,443 --> 00:28:47,611
I know, right?

368
00:28:54,076 --> 00:28:56,286
Have you eaten?

369
00:29:01,542 --> 00:29:02,668
I met

370
00:29:04,253 --> 00:29:06,630
Jinu and Teo at the police station.

371
00:29:07,297 --> 00:29:08,507
The police station?

372
00:29:09,800 --> 00:29:11,927
They got hacked

373
00:29:12,761 --> 00:29:15,180
and the data
was all about D.N.X's comeback.

374
00:29:18,100 --> 00:29:19,726
They still haven't given up
on that dream.

375
00:29:22,187 --> 00:29:23,814
I didn't know they were so desperate.

376
00:29:28,402 --> 00:29:29,945
But you feel the same way.

377
00:29:32,322 --> 00:29:35,784
Wasn't that why you had been
working on that fan song?

378
00:29:42,332 --> 00:29:43,876
You're right.

379
00:29:48,130 --> 00:29:49,673
But I guess I must have no courage.

380
00:29:50,465 --> 00:29:54,261
The courage to throw away
great opportunities

381
00:29:55,429 --> 00:29:56,889
and my career.

382
00:29:59,433 --> 00:30:02,895
Is it because
that's the practical choice?

383
00:30:13,113 --> 00:30:15,073
I should focus on my movie, right?

384
00:30:21,580 --> 00:30:22,664
Whatever choice you make

385
00:30:24,208 --> 00:30:26,460
I want you to do

386
00:30:27,586 --> 00:30:28,754
what your heart tells you to do.

387
00:30:30,672 --> 00:30:32,382
Something for yourself.

388
00:30:49,608 --> 00:30:50,901
<i>Whatever choice you make</i>

389
00:30:51,401 --> 00:30:55,113
<i>I want you to do
what your heart tells you to do.</i>

390
00:30:55,948 --> 00:30:57,616
<i>Something for yourself.</i>

391
00:31:28,563 --> 00:31:31,066
- All right!
- Come with me.

392
00:31:32,985 --> 00:31:34,611
I'm over here.

393
00:31:40,867 --> 00:31:41,868
Ms. Da-reum.

394
00:31:42,411 --> 00:31:43,412
Look.

395
00:31:52,879 --> 00:31:54,047
What is this?

396
00:31:55,048 --> 00:31:57,718
It's so pretty. What is this?

397
00:31:58,260 --> 00:32:00,554
My gosh. Did you prepare all this?

398
00:32:05,434 --> 00:32:07,311
How pretty.

399
00:32:07,394 --> 00:32:09,396
When did you look these up
and prepare everything?

400
00:32:10,731 --> 00:32:11,940
Well, you know.

401
00:32:12,649 --> 00:32:13,859
I just saw it by coincidence.

402
00:32:15,527 --> 00:32:16,611
Is that true?

403
00:32:20,240 --> 00:32:21,408
Try this.

404
00:32:27,581 --> 00:32:29,166
- Do you like it?
- This is good too.

405
00:32:44,890 --> 00:32:48,143
The weekend feels so short.

406
00:32:50,520 --> 00:32:51,938
I don't want to go to work tomorrow.

407
00:32:56,777 --> 00:32:58,403
How can you say that
in front of your CEO?

408
00:32:59,237 --> 00:33:00,238
What?

409
00:33:02,407 --> 00:33:03,742
I was talking to my boyfriend.

410
00:33:29,935 --> 00:33:31,186
4 P.M. GO TO THE LAKE
5 P.M. WATCH THE REFLECTION

411
00:33:36,400 --> 00:33:38,860
Do you want to move to the lake?

412
00:33:38,944 --> 00:33:40,862
- Why?
- Because...

413
00:33:41,696 --> 00:33:43,156
I heard it's beautiful at sunset.

414
00:33:43,698 --> 00:33:44,866
To show me the light reflection?

415
00:33:47,953 --> 00:33:50,789
But I just want to stay here.

416
00:34:06,763 --> 00:34:08,265
1 P.M. LUNCH AT THE RESTAURANT
2 P.M. CAFE

417
00:34:08,348 --> 00:34:10,016
3 P.M. PICNIC ON THE GRASS
4 P.M. GO TO THE LAKE

418
00:34:12,936 --> 00:34:14,896
We don't have to move
according to your plan.

419
00:34:18,066 --> 00:34:20,610
Why are you trying so hard
to impress me today?

420
00:34:23,196 --> 00:34:26,908
I didn't get to meet
your friends properly last time.

421
00:34:28,702 --> 00:34:29,911
And we haven't seen
each other lately.

422
00:34:29,995 --> 00:34:31,163
Did that bother you?

423
00:34:34,875 --> 00:34:37,878
I wanted to do it right this time.

424
00:34:40,088 --> 00:34:43,675
It's because of Ms. Han, isn't it?

425
00:34:49,139 --> 00:34:51,475
- I...
- You said I had nothing to worry.

426
00:34:52,684 --> 00:34:57,189
I decided to take on HAN
because I trust you.

427
00:34:58,148 --> 00:35:00,025
You don't have to try that hard.

428
00:35:00,108 --> 00:35:01,818
I just like it when we're together.

429
00:35:13,121 --> 00:35:14,247
Thank you.

430
00:35:18,668 --> 00:35:19,711
Do you want to lie down again?

431
00:35:20,545 --> 00:35:22,422
No, I want to stay like this.

432
00:35:30,013 --> 00:35:32,432
<i>Beyond the forgotten memories</i>

433
00:35:33,099 --> 00:35:35,143
<i>I want to go up into the sky</i>

434
00:35:36,061 --> 00:35:37,187
<i>Get on</i>

435
00:35:39,397 --> 00:35:40,565
Oh, gosh.

436
00:35:43,443 --> 00:35:45,237
It's been so long
that I don't remember anything.

437
00:35:46,321 --> 00:35:48,448
You're getting old.

438
00:35:48,698 --> 00:35:50,158
Wait till you're my age.

439
00:35:50,242 --> 00:35:52,244
It's not easy to dance like this.

440
00:35:52,410 --> 00:35:55,705
Anyway, it's so nice
to practice together.

441
00:35:55,789 --> 00:35:58,917
- Me too.
- You're grossing me out. Get off me.

442
00:36:00,210 --> 00:36:01,878
It would've been nice
if Chan was here.

443
00:36:10,053 --> 00:36:12,138
Don't get your hopes up.

444
00:36:13,265 --> 00:36:15,600
D.N.X means nothing
to a top star like him.

445
00:36:16,601 --> 00:36:18,144
He's on his way to Hollywood.

446
00:36:20,814 --> 00:36:22,190
Why don't we try it again?

447
00:36:23,066 --> 00:36:24,401
Let's start from "Get on."

448
00:36:38,039 --> 00:36:40,834
MYEONGMYEONG BUILDING

449
00:36:43,962 --> 00:36:49,050
{\an8}MYU DANCE STUDIO

450
00:37:20,248 --> 00:37:21,291
Roy.

451
00:37:23,835 --> 00:37:26,046
I don't care who you like.

452
00:37:27,756 --> 00:37:28,757
But

453
00:37:29,841 --> 00:37:32,010
it's too much for us
to handle right now.

454
00:37:34,679 --> 00:37:35,680
Let's keep it a secret.

455
00:37:37,474 --> 00:37:38,558
Later...

456
00:37:40,185 --> 00:37:41,770
When things get better...

457
00:37:43,938 --> 00:37:45,065
Just until then.

458
00:37:50,695 --> 00:37:51,738
Okay.

459
00:38:01,706 --> 00:38:04,250
SHOCKING PICTURES OF ROY
AND HIS BOYFRIEND

460
00:38:08,338 --> 00:38:10,757
DARK CLOUDS OVER D.N.X,
ALL EYES ON THEIR FUTURE

461
00:38:11,174 --> 00:38:12,217
Stop reading it.

462
00:38:13,677 --> 00:38:16,346
- Chan, what do we do now?
- That's why I told you...

463
00:38:18,723 --> 00:38:20,642
You should've been more careful, Roy.

464
00:38:26,314 --> 00:38:27,565
<i>Roy!</i>

465
00:38:27,649 --> 00:38:29,484
- Hey.
- Don't do this to Roy.

466
00:38:29,567 --> 00:38:31,444
- Stop.
- Move. Get out of my way!

467
00:38:31,528 --> 00:38:33,446
- Don't do this too.
- I said, move!

468
00:38:35,240 --> 00:38:36,658
You're no different.

469
00:38:36,950 --> 00:38:39,369
The two of you ruined
everything we built!

470
00:39:01,057 --> 00:39:02,892
{\an8}QUICK DELIVERY

471
00:39:02,976 --> 00:39:05,562
- Hi, I'm back.
- Good job today.

472
00:39:06,604 --> 00:39:09,774
Hey, the boss saw him.
He really is a celebrity.

473
00:39:09,858 --> 00:39:13,153
He was a member of some group
called D.N. something.

474
00:39:13,236 --> 00:39:17,157
- Don't be ridiculous.
- But it's true. I swear.

475
00:39:17,407 --> 00:39:18,700
- Want to bet 50,000 won?
- You called it.

476
00:39:18,783 --> 00:39:20,076
- Yes.
- Deal.

477
00:39:20,160 --> 00:39:22,287
You said 50,000 won.

478
00:39:28,334 --> 00:39:31,296
Hey, take off your helmet
for a second.

479
00:39:31,379 --> 00:39:34,215
We've worked together for months,
but I still haven't seen your face.

480
00:39:34,299 --> 00:39:35,800
Hey, I heard you were an idol.

481
00:39:35,884 --> 00:39:37,927
- Is it true? Show me.
- No.

482
00:39:38,011 --> 00:39:39,971
- Hey, take it off.
- Take it off, will you?

483
00:39:40,054 --> 00:39:42,766
- Why won't you take it off?
- Let me see your face.

484
00:39:45,393 --> 00:39:48,396
Seriously, don't you have
anything else to do?

485
00:39:50,607 --> 00:39:53,276
What on earth are you doing
when you should be

486
00:39:53,359 --> 00:39:54,778
working hard at this busy hour?

487
00:39:54,861 --> 00:39:55,904
Who are you?

488
00:40:00,408 --> 00:40:01,659
Triple the delivery fee.

489
00:40:02,410 --> 00:40:03,870
There's a limited time event.

490
00:40:04,496 --> 00:40:05,789
TRIPLE THE DELIVERY FEE
TIME EVENT

491
00:40:06,998 --> 00:40:09,000
- It's true.
- I can't miss this.

492
00:40:09,083 --> 00:40:10,543
I'll see you when I come back.

493
00:40:10,794 --> 00:40:13,129
It's only on for two hours.

494
00:40:16,257 --> 00:40:18,009
Stop bothering him.

495
00:40:19,427 --> 00:40:20,428
Thank you.

496
00:40:23,556 --> 00:40:25,225
Then can you make some time for me?

497
00:40:38,780 --> 00:40:39,989
Thank you, Seul-a.

498
00:40:41,282 --> 00:40:43,409
That's all you drink.

499
00:40:45,078 --> 00:40:46,412
How did you know?

500
00:40:47,247 --> 00:40:48,540
Because I was your fan.

501
00:40:50,333 --> 00:40:52,001
No, it's not that I was.

502
00:40:52,502 --> 00:40:53,962
I still am.

503
00:40:57,841 --> 00:41:01,845
I started
this delivery job to find you.

504
00:41:03,179 --> 00:41:05,932
- What?
- To see if it really was you.

505
00:41:06,349 --> 00:41:07,392
Then I realized it was you.

506
00:41:12,480 --> 00:41:16,526
Honestly, I don't care what you do.

507
00:41:17,652 --> 00:41:19,445
But you never take the helmet off.

508
00:41:22,156 --> 00:41:23,867
That really upsets me.

509
00:41:25,535 --> 00:41:29,163
I know that you feel bad
about what happened to the team.

510
00:41:32,333 --> 00:41:33,793
But I don't want you

511
00:41:35,169 --> 00:41:38,298
to live as if you never existed
just because of that.

512
00:41:40,091 --> 00:41:42,510
I've never been ashamed of you.

513
00:41:42,844 --> 00:41:44,679
Back then or now.

514
00:41:45,847 --> 00:41:46,890
So...

515
00:41:48,808 --> 00:41:51,394
don't hide yourself,
at least from me.

516
00:42:47,116 --> 00:42:50,703
I made a list of pop-up stores
that would fit HAN's concept.

517
00:42:53,289 --> 00:42:55,124
I like the space.

518
00:42:55,208 --> 00:42:56,459
The location is good.

519
00:42:56,542 --> 00:42:59,671
Only global luxury brands have held
pop-up stores there.

520
00:42:59,754 --> 00:43:01,714
There's intense competition
for the space, not just from us.

521
00:43:02,090 --> 00:43:03,508
It must've required a lot of legwork.

522
00:43:04,342 --> 00:43:05,343
Not at all.

523
00:43:07,136 --> 00:43:08,262
However

524
00:43:09,722 --> 00:43:11,307
the streets may be crowded

525
00:43:11,808 --> 00:43:13,559
but none of them are my customers.

526
00:43:14,811 --> 00:43:15,812
I beg your pardon?

527
00:43:17,230 --> 00:43:19,899
Is this all you prepared?

528
00:43:29,826 --> 00:43:31,119
PROJECT PROPOSAL

529
00:43:34,414 --> 00:43:35,623
Wait.

530
00:43:38,084 --> 00:43:41,212
Actually, aside from the places
you saw in the meeting

531
00:43:41,754 --> 00:43:43,965
I have another one in mind.

532
00:43:55,351 --> 00:43:56,436
Where are we?

533
00:43:58,062 --> 00:43:59,147
This is Ikseon-dong.

534
00:44:01,482 --> 00:44:03,067
I looked into why HAN's main branch
in Paris is

535
00:44:03,526 --> 00:44:07,071
located in the old streets
of Saint-Germain

536
00:44:07,155 --> 00:44:10,491
instead of Rue Saint-Honoré,
where all the luxury brands are.

537
00:44:11,492 --> 00:44:14,454
It's a place with unique cafes,
private bookstores

538
00:44:14,871 --> 00:44:16,205
and a lot of vintage shops.

539
00:44:16,706 --> 00:44:19,667
It's where people
with a strong sense of style go.

540
00:44:20,460 --> 00:44:23,171
I thought about where those people
would go in Korea.

541
00:44:24,380 --> 00:44:25,381
And?

542
00:44:25,798 --> 00:44:27,925
My impression is that HAN's customers

543
00:44:28,593 --> 00:44:31,804
like to walk, explore, and stay.

544
00:44:33,264 --> 00:44:37,143
They buy something
that reflects what they like.

545
00:44:39,479 --> 00:44:42,690
I'm finally starting to like it.

546
00:44:45,777 --> 00:44:46,778
Sure.

547
00:44:47,236 --> 00:44:49,197
Let's keep looking around.

548
00:44:52,366 --> 00:44:53,576
Yes, Ms. Han.

549
00:44:59,290 --> 00:45:01,417
My first brand didn't work out.

550
00:45:02,627 --> 00:45:04,670
Then is HAN your second one?

551
00:45:06,589 --> 00:45:08,883
I started it with a friend
from fashion school

552
00:45:09,425 --> 00:45:10,927
and we got good responses
when we first opened.

553
00:45:12,386 --> 00:45:13,471
Then why didn't it work out?

554
00:45:15,014 --> 00:45:17,308
My friend went behind my back

555
00:45:17,391 --> 00:45:19,060
and I lost everything
to a major corporation.

556
00:45:19,977 --> 00:45:21,813
I started from scratch again.

557
00:45:22,438 --> 00:45:23,731
That led to HAN now.

558
00:45:27,568 --> 00:45:28,903
It must've been tough.

559
00:45:29,654 --> 00:45:32,448
It was, but that helped me grow up.

560
00:45:33,324 --> 00:45:37,078
It taught me what I was capable of.

561
00:45:37,829 --> 00:45:40,373
I realized I was relying
on her sense a lot

562
00:45:40,665 --> 00:45:41,999
and not my own.

563
00:45:43,626 --> 00:45:46,921
So when I started HAN,
I focused on myself

564
00:45:47,755 --> 00:45:51,676
like what I could present
and what I was good at.

565
00:45:54,220 --> 00:45:56,722
<i>She's undeniably cool.</i>

566
00:45:59,642 --> 00:46:01,018
What about you, Ms. Da-reum?

567
00:46:01,686 --> 00:46:05,314
Do you feel like the work you do
at Appello is truly yours?

568
00:46:09,652 --> 00:46:14,031
I'm still learning.
I think I'm getting there.

569
00:46:18,452 --> 00:46:19,537
By any chance

570
00:46:20,788 --> 00:46:23,416
does my relationship
with Mr. Kang bother you?

571
00:46:32,550 --> 00:46:36,012
I'd be lying if I said no.

572
00:46:37,430 --> 00:46:38,848
That's very honest.

573
00:46:38,931 --> 00:46:39,974
But I...

574
00:46:40,808 --> 00:46:42,643
I trust the person I'm dating.

575
00:46:47,773 --> 00:46:48,816
Do you?

576
00:47:00,161 --> 00:47:01,787
<i>In the end</i>

577
00:47:01,871 --> 00:47:04,624
HAN's customers must be those
who are drawn to scarcity.

578
00:47:08,586 --> 00:47:09,879
Come on.

579
00:47:10,922 --> 00:47:12,465
What are you so worried about?

580
00:47:20,389 --> 00:47:23,267
Ms. Han Jeong-yeon seems kind to us.

581
00:47:23,351 --> 00:47:24,518
You shouldn't worry so much.

582
00:47:28,522 --> 00:47:29,649
Seong-wook.

583
00:47:30,483 --> 00:47:33,653
SE's ideas are too similar to ours.

584
00:47:36,864 --> 00:47:41,118
But it's normal for ideas like that
to overlap in this field.

585
00:47:41,953 --> 00:47:44,163
Hey, don't you think
you're being too sensitive lately?

586
00:47:47,500 --> 00:47:49,126
I wish that was the case.

587
00:47:51,379 --> 00:47:52,922
Don't worry.

588
00:47:59,720 --> 00:48:02,181
Come on.
There's nothing to worry about.

589
00:48:03,182 --> 00:48:04,225
Okay?

590
00:48:04,892 --> 00:48:05,893
Right.

591
00:48:08,521 --> 00:48:10,731
Thank you for everything today.
I appreciate it.

592
00:48:12,149 --> 00:48:14,318
Is there anything else
I can help you with?

593
00:48:15,319 --> 00:48:17,196
It's okay. I'm expecting someone.

594
00:48:18,364 --> 00:48:22,493
- Bye now.
- Okay, I'll see you later.

595
00:48:45,516 --> 00:48:49,520
I'm going to tell him
I pulled it off today.

596
00:48:57,028 --> 00:48:59,864
<i>The person you're trying to reach
is not available.</i>

597
00:48:59,947 --> 00:49:02,241
<i>Please leave a message
after the beep.</i>

598
00:49:43,199 --> 00:49:44,700
ANNUAL PERFORMANCE REPORT

599
00:49:44,784 --> 00:49:47,203
SE CORPORATION QUARTERLY PERFORMANCE
BY DIVISION

600
00:49:50,581 --> 00:49:52,166
{\an8}ILLEGAL SUBCONTRACT
INVESTIGATION REPORT

601
00:49:52,249 --> 00:49:54,001
SE CORPORATION BUSINESS ANALYSIS

602
00:49:54,085 --> 00:49:55,878
CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION LEAK

603
00:50:04,929 --> 00:50:08,891
SE spent too much on marketing
after starting their platform.

604
00:50:10,559 --> 00:50:11,727
It's like they were gambling.

605
00:50:12,478 --> 00:50:13,562
How did you secure this?

606
00:50:14,063 --> 00:50:16,023
Through the agency
that consulted SE: ON.

607
00:50:16,315 --> 00:50:19,610
I've been tracking their movement
since before I came to Korea.

608
00:50:22,029 --> 00:50:23,823
It's always the same for SE.

609
00:50:24,657 --> 00:50:27,576
They call it
collaboration and investment

610
00:50:28,577 --> 00:50:30,621
but all they're thinking about
is taking over other companies.

611
00:50:34,542 --> 00:50:35,793
I know it from experience.

612
00:50:39,171 --> 00:50:40,923
They approached us the same way.

613
00:50:49,932 --> 00:50:51,642
MS. NAM DA-REUM:
WHERE ARE YOU?

614
00:50:52,017 --> 00:50:53,769
I JUST FINISHED

615
00:51:11,412 --> 00:51:13,330
WHERE ARE YOU?
I JUST FINISHED

616
00:51:21,505 --> 00:51:24,049
CEO KANG HA-GI OF APPELLO

617
00:51:31,223 --> 00:51:32,975
I can't even call him.

618
00:51:38,481 --> 00:51:39,690
I'm so pathetic.

619
00:51:43,944 --> 00:51:45,613
CHAN

620
00:51:52,828 --> 00:51:54,705
- Hi, Chan.
- <i>What are you up to, Da-reum?</i>

621
00:51:56,707 --> 00:51:58,709
Nothing much.

622
00:51:59,335 --> 00:52:00,669
Then do you want to listen to this?

623
00:52:02,838 --> 00:52:03,923
Listen to what?

624
00:52:05,466 --> 00:52:06,550
One second.

625
00:52:55,140 --> 00:52:56,141
What do you think?

626
00:52:58,477 --> 00:53:00,437
I love it.

627
00:53:02,022 --> 00:53:06,277
It feels comforting.

628
00:53:09,321 --> 00:53:11,699
I've been stuck,
but you helped me work through it.

629
00:53:12,741 --> 00:53:13,826
I did?

630
00:53:13,909 --> 00:53:16,996
<i>I just went with my heart
like you said.</i>

631
00:53:18,914 --> 00:53:22,334
Go with my heart...

632
00:53:24,878 --> 00:53:26,380
I should've done this earlier.

633
00:53:27,506 --> 00:53:28,674
<i>Thanks, Da-reum.</i>

634
00:53:32,970 --> 00:53:34,555
I said that...

635
00:53:36,599 --> 00:53:38,225
when I couldn't even do it myself.

636
00:53:39,101 --> 00:53:40,311
<i>What's that?</i>

637
00:53:42,104 --> 00:53:43,355
Nothing.

638
00:53:43,439 --> 00:53:45,983
Let me hear it when you're done.

639
00:53:46,400 --> 00:53:48,068
I'm sorry. I have to go.

640
00:54:22,478 --> 00:54:23,854
Want a glass?

641
00:54:26,774 --> 00:54:27,775
No, thanks.

642
00:54:31,236 --> 00:54:32,863
When can I talk to you again

643
00:54:33,572 --> 00:54:35,115
not as the CEO of Appello

644
00:54:35,949 --> 00:54:37,660
but as Kang Ha-gi?

645
00:54:39,328 --> 00:54:40,412
Next time.

646
00:54:40,996 --> 00:54:41,997
With Chan too.

647
00:54:55,427 --> 00:54:57,221
MISSED CALL
MS. NAM DA-REUM

648
00:55:16,281 --> 00:55:17,366
<i>By any chance</i>

649
00:55:18,409 --> 00:55:20,828
<i>does my relationship
with Mr. Kang bother you?</i>

650
00:55:23,247 --> 00:55:24,415
<i>But I...</i>

651
00:55:25,499 --> 00:55:27,418
<i>I trust the person I'm dating.</i>

652
00:55:30,379 --> 00:55:31,422
Do you?

653
00:55:32,381 --> 00:55:34,174
<i>It's okay. I'm expecting someone.</i>

654
00:56:17,050 --> 00:56:18,218
Is it too late?

655
00:56:20,012 --> 00:56:21,221
I missed you.

656
00:56:30,189 --> 00:56:31,190
What's wrong?

657
00:56:32,524 --> 00:56:33,609
Is something the matter?

658
00:56:36,445 --> 00:56:37,446
Yes.

659
00:56:38,864 --> 00:56:39,907
I saw you

660
00:56:40,699 --> 00:56:43,160
entering Ms. Han's hotel earlier.

661
00:56:47,414 --> 00:56:50,501
Were you with her all this while?

662
00:56:56,089 --> 00:56:58,217
- I...
- You didn't tell me.

663
00:56:58,884 --> 00:57:00,344
And I couldn't reach you.

664
00:57:02,346 --> 00:57:05,015
If I hadn't seen you, I wouldn't have
known you were together.

665
00:57:05,349 --> 00:57:07,392
- It's a misunderstanding.
- If it's not, what is it?

666
00:57:15,275 --> 00:57:16,318
Later.

667
00:57:17,277 --> 00:57:18,487
I'll tell you later.

668
00:57:24,535 --> 00:57:25,577
I'm sorry.

669
00:57:31,959 --> 00:57:33,043
But I'm...

670
00:57:35,087 --> 00:57:38,257
I'm your girlfriend.

671
00:57:40,676 --> 00:57:43,095
How am I different from a stranger?

672
00:57:46,640 --> 00:57:47,641
Ms. Da-reum...

673
00:57:52,896 --> 00:57:53,939
I'm sorry.

674
00:57:55,816 --> 00:57:57,860
I can't pretend to be okay right now.

675
00:59:05,719 --> 00:59:07,846
- It's the final presentation data.
- Okay.

676
00:59:07,930 --> 00:59:09,348
CUSTOMER PROFILING REPORT
APPELLO

677
00:59:19,107 --> 00:59:20,275
But Mr. Kang

678
00:59:20,943 --> 00:59:23,820
this is completely different from
what we discussed in the meeting.

679
00:59:23,904 --> 00:59:24,905
Why did it change?

680
00:59:25,447 --> 00:59:26,823
I leaked that on purpose.

681
00:59:27,950 --> 00:59:29,117
This is the real data.

682
00:59:31,828 --> 00:59:33,455
We have to be careful
until the presentation.

683
00:59:36,959 --> 00:59:38,168
Please go over it.

684
00:59:39,878 --> 00:59:41,129
Yes, sir.

685
01:00:06,029 --> 01:00:07,114
Hello.

686
01:00:37,394 --> 01:00:39,146
They must've had a fight, right?

687
01:00:39,229 --> 01:00:40,772
Isn't this the first time
since they started dating?

688
01:00:40,856 --> 01:00:42,941
It's so obvious. It's suffocating me.

689
01:00:44,443 --> 01:00:46,695
I can feel it.

690
01:00:47,070 --> 01:00:48,071
What now?

691
01:00:48,739 --> 01:00:51,074
Maybe they're faking it,
so they won't get caught.

692
01:00:53,577 --> 01:00:54,703
What?

693
01:00:55,662 --> 01:00:56,788
But it's true.

694
01:00:57,372 --> 01:00:59,291
I'm very sharp, you know?

695
01:01:06,089 --> 01:01:07,132
Da-reum.

696
01:01:09,217 --> 01:01:12,596
- There you are.
- Are you here to see me?

697
01:01:12,679 --> 01:01:14,931
Yes, you said you wanted to hear
the fan song when it was ready.

698
01:01:15,682 --> 01:01:16,683
Oh, right.

699
01:01:20,270 --> 01:01:22,856
You didn't sound well last time
I talked to you on the phone.

700
01:01:22,939 --> 01:01:24,608
I was also worried if you were okay.

701
01:01:26,777 --> 01:01:29,154
I'm fine.
There's nothing to worry about.

702
01:01:30,822 --> 01:01:32,866
Should we listen to it
in the showroom? There are speakers.

703
01:01:33,366 --> 01:01:34,409
Sure.

704
01:01:39,790 --> 01:01:41,625
- Can you put it on bluetooth?
- Yes.

705
01:01:42,167 --> 01:01:43,668
SETTINGS

706
01:01:44,044 --> 01:01:48,173
I don't think she's caught on
to what we've been up to yet.

707
01:01:48,632 --> 01:01:50,467
I'm going to tell her the truth.

708
01:03:24,436 --> 01:03:28,190
{\an8}MY BIAS, MY BOSS

709
01:03:38,783 --> 01:03:41,453
{\an8}- It's the same, down to every word.
- This is crazy.

710
01:03:41,536 --> 01:03:43,288
{\an8}How can it be the same?

711
01:03:43,872 --> 01:03:46,333
{\an8}<i>Mr. Kang didn't come to work today.</i>

712
01:03:46,416 --> 01:03:48,001
{\an8}<i>He never once missed work</i>

713
01:03:48,084 --> 01:03:49,419
{\an8}<i>rain or shine,
or even when he was sick.</i>

714
01:03:50,587 --> 01:03:52,505
{\an8}<i>I'll stay by your side to the end.</i>

715
01:03:54,216 --> 01:03:55,717
{\an8}<i>There's something I want to do.</i>

716
01:03:56,092 --> 01:03:57,510
{\an8}<i>We never waited for you.</i>

717
01:03:58,803 --> 01:04:01,097
{\an8}<i>I didn't want to hide it anymore.</i>

718
01:04:01,181 --> 01:04:02,182
{\an8}I LOVE LEE CHAN

719
01:04:02,265 --> 01:04:03,600
{\an8}<i>I wanted to show you</i>

720
01:04:04,351 --> 01:04:07,020
{\an8}<i>that this is who I am,
and the part of me that loves you</i>

721
01:04:08,188 --> 01:04:09,522
{\an8}<i>is also a part of who I am.</i>

722
01:04:15,159 --> 01:04:17,161
{\an8}Subtitles by Eunjin Erica Kim
and Jennifer Jean Lim

723
01:04:17,242 --> 01:04:19,244
